================================================================================
NVIDIA NVRTC -- the CUDA runtime compiler (NOT part of this package)
================================================================================

crow-nest does not distribute any NVIDIA file. The engine package holds serve
(serve.exe), LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, and nothing from
NVIDIA; tools/pack-engine.ps1 and tools/pack-engine.sh refuse to build a
package that holds one.

At run time serve loads NVIDIA's runtime compilation library (NVRTC) to compile
its CUDA kernels, and needs NVRTC 13.3.33, the build the engine's PTX manifest
was recorded with. You obtain it from NVIDIA yourself: NVIDIA publishes NVRTC as
the `nvidia-cuda-nvrtc` 13.3.33 wheel on PyPI, and tools/fetch-nvrtc.ps1
(Windows) or tools/fetch-nvrtc.sh (Linux) downloads that wheel straight from
files.pythonhosted.org, checks it against the pinned size and sha256 and
against the wheel's own RECORD, and places these files beside serve:

    Windows   nvrtc64_130_0.dll, nvrtc-builtins64_133.dll
    Linux     libnvrtc.so (the bytes of the wheel's libnvrtc.so.13, under the
              unversioned name cudarc loads first), libnvrtc-builtins.so.13.3

NVRTC is NVIDIA's software. It is not covered by the Apache-2.0 grant in
LICENSE, and your use of it is under the licence terms NVIDIA ships with it
(the wheel and the NVIDIA Software License Agreement and CUDA Supplement to
Software License Agreement, the CUDA Toolkit EULA,
https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/index.html). Questions about those terms go
to NVIDIA.
